Scope carve-out — what the MIT license above covers, and what it does not

The MIT grant above applies to the project's own material only: this
documentation set (README, docs/, agent.md, analysis/, skills/), the build and
verification scripts, and the project's descriptions of the analyzed package.

It does NOT apply to the contents of the analyzed APK itself, which are
included in this repository in extracted and decompiled form for research and
interoperability purposes only:

- The base application is Alight Motion, Copyright (c) Alight Creative LLC
  (with later-era components associated with Bending Spoons). All original
  application code, resources, assets, native libraries, and trademarks
  remain the property of their respective owners. Nothing in this repository
  is authored by, endorsed by, or affiliated with Alight Creative LLC.
- The modification layer ("Gold Motion", attributed to the modder "PNKJ"),
  including its branding assets, custom effects, AI models, and added code, is
  likewise the work of its respective author(s) and is documented here without
  endorsement. Where those components embed third-party works (e.g. published
  AI models), the upstream licenses of those works continue to apply.

The decompiled representations in extracted-format/ and decompiled/ are
derivative artifacts produced mechanically from the redistributed APK. They
are provided for study, education, and interoperability research; no
ownership claim is made over them, and redistribution of the APK or its
contents does not confer any rights beyond what applicable law (including any
copyright exceptions for study and interoperability) already provides. If you
are a rights holder and believe material is included improperly, please open
an issue in this repository's issue tracker.
